ed to detach from origin_availability_alpha to make it available, then attach to shift_candidate_beta, then maybe re-attach to origin? But origin needs to stay linked for its own goal? Actually goal does not require origin_availability_alpha to have task profile linked? Wait goal includes (candidate_task_profile_linked shift_candidate_beta route_task_profile_alpha) but does not require origin_availability_alpha to have it linked. However initial has it linked; we could detach and not reattach; but then we might break other conditions that depend on origin_availability_alpha having task profile linked? Let's see what else uses candidate_task_profile_linked for origin_availability_alpha: There are actions like activate_origin_node, assign_compliance_certificate, lock_origin_availability, etc. They have precondition (candidate_prepared ?origin_availability) and (candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile). Indeed many actions require candidate_task_profile_linked for origin_availability_alpha. For example, activate_origin_node requires candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile. Also assign_compliance_certificate, lock_origin_availability, etc. So we need to keep that link for origin_availability_alpha to satisfy those preconditions needed for achieving goal conditions like origin_availability_locked, origin_availability_confirmed, dispatch_allocated, dispatch_ready, dispatched, etc. Indeed many actions for origin_availability_alpha require the task profile link. So we must keep it linked.)
